WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.099 --> 00:00:04.430
Speaker 1: One of the incredible things that
has happened in the context of the Russian

00:00:04.430 --> 00:00:11.600
invasion of Ukraine is that much of the world
has become united against Russia and in defense

00:00:11.600 --> 00:00:12.600
of Ukraine.

00:00:12.600 --> 00:00:18.480
You look at the list of countries now sending
military support, weapons support rather to

00:00:18.480 --> 00:00:19.480
Ukraine.

00:00:19.480 --> 00:00:25.240
It's an incredible list and with some rare
exceptions, I mean, you know, Belarus and

00:00:25.240 --> 00:00:29.320
you know, the typical handful of exceptions.

00:00:29.320 --> 00:00:35.870
Much of the world has not been as united for
or against anything as we have seen over the

00:00:35.870 --> 00:00:36.870
last week.

00:00:36.870 --> 00:00:43.100
And as I've said before, the Ukrainian President
Zelensky was not particularly popular before

00:00:43.100 --> 00:00:49.339
this started, and there are still all sorts
of concerns when it comes to corruption in

00:00:49.339 --> 00:00:51.469
Ukraine, as we've talked about before.

00:00:51.469 --> 00:00:54.420
But the degree to which he has become.

00:00:54.420 --> 00:00:58.019
Quite often, I say as a joke.

00:00:58.019 --> 00:01:04.030
Defiant and principled, but he has remained
defiant and principled in a way that people

00:01:04.030 --> 00:01:07.860
the world over are really rallying behind.

00:01:07.860 --> 00:01:15.170
And most recently with a quite frankly, of
irate viral speech to European Parliament,

00:01:15.170 --> 00:01:23.810
during which you'll hear the translator become
audibly emotional, leading to a minute long

00:01:23.810 --> 00:01:26.509
standing ovation after the second clip.

00:01:26.509 --> 00:01:30.820
Let's take a listen, and this is the voice
of the translator that you will hear.

00:01:30.820 --> 00:01:39.960
Speaker 2: We are fighting just for our land
and for our freedom.

00:01:39.960 --> 00:01:50.200
Despite the fact that all large cities of
our country are now blocked, nobody is going

00:01:50.200 --> 00:01:53.560
to enter and intervene with our freedom and
country.

00:01:53.560 --> 00:01:55.150
And believe you me.

00:01:55.150 --> 00:02:03.159
Every square today, no matter what it's called,
it's going to be called as today, Freedom

00:02:03.159 --> 00:02:08.110
Square in every city of our country.

00:02:08.110 --> 00:02:09.320
Nobody is going to break us.

00:02:09.320 --> 00:02:10.660
We are strong.

00:02:10.660 --> 00:02:11.990
We are Ukrainians.

00:02:11.990 --> 00:02:20.970
Speaker 1: And of course, the hope would be
that indeed, Ukraine will be able to repel

00:02:20.970 --> 00:02:23.290
the invasion from Russia.

00:02:23.290 --> 00:02:24.940
We don't know that know that yet.

00:02:24.940 --> 00:02:30.580
And if it doesn't happen, it will not be from
lack of desire or resolve.

00:02:30.580 --> 00:02:35.780
It will be because of the sheer size of the
Russian military.

00:02:35.780 --> 00:02:41.900
And the most recent reports are that Kharkiv
is increasingly surrounded.

00:02:41.900 --> 00:02:48.060
And you know, it's so hard to know what is
really going on because many of the reports

00:02:48.060 --> 00:02:55.320
that have come out later are retracted or
were based on confused or incorrect information.

00:02:55.320 --> 00:03:00.620
But the desire is there, and here is more
from the Ukrainian President Selenski ending

00:03:00.620 --> 00:03:05.090
his speech before European Parliament to a
minute long standing ovation.

00:03:05.090 --> 00:03:09.030
Speaker 2: So do prove that you are with us.

00:03:09.030 --> 00:03:14.290
Do prove that you will not let us go.

00:03:14.290 --> 00:03:24.340
Do prove that you indeed are Europeans and
then life will win over death and light will

00:03:24.340 --> 00:03:26.870
win over darkness.

00:03:26.870 --> 00:03:34.310
Glory be to Ukraine.

00:03:34.310 --> 00:03:51.560
Speaker 1: So as you can tell, quite a united
planet at this point in time, and there are,

00:03:51.560 --> 00:03:55.980
as always, conflicting reports coming out
of Russia, on the one hand, when it comes

00:03:55.980 --> 00:04:00.320
to the military front, like I just said reports
that Kharkiv is in an increasingly precarious

00:04:00.320 --> 00:04:05.290
situation as of the last three or four hours
surrounded and that things are not looking

00:04:05.290 --> 00:04:06.290
good.

00:04:06.290 --> 00:04:12.761
At the same time, there are multiple reports
that Putin's grip, so to speak on power, may

00:04:12.761 --> 00:04:16.220
be starting to slip, at least ideologically.

00:04:16.220 --> 00:04:21.680
Yahoo News Daily Beast article Rather, the
Russian people may be starting to think Putin

00:04:21.680 --> 00:04:24.940
is insane, and I encourage you.

00:04:24.940 --> 00:04:29.060
I mean, listen, I encourage people to read
all of the things that are being written and

00:04:29.060 --> 00:04:34.630
understand that what really happened if we
will ever fully know the story, it's only

00:04:34.630 --> 00:04:36.900
going to be in retrospect.

00:04:36.900 --> 00:04:45.620
But we will, of course, continue covering
what is going on and hope, hope that indeed,

00:04:45.620 --> 00:04:53.240
Ukrainian forces and allies are going to be
able to repeal repel this horrifying invasion.

00:04:53.240 --> 00:04:56.830
And we will continue talking about what the
what the next steps may be.

00:04:56.830 --> 00:05:00.210
And quite frankly, Joe Biden's State of the
Union address tonight, which we'll be covering

00:05:00.210 --> 00:05:02.930
live, may give us some of that information.

00:05:02.930 --> 00:05:06.139
In the meantime, there's much more to talk
about here, and I want to talk next about

00:05:06.139 --> 00:05:10.030
an incredible statement made by the Ukrainian
ambassador to the United Nations.

